{% comment %}
  RAQI Redesign — §3A Homepage hero. LOCKED, signed off. Do not restyle.

  Single static composition. No carousel, no rotation, no dot indicators.
  The ENTIRE hero — both columns — is one click target linking to the Discovery
  Set builder at /pages/discovery-box.

  NOTE: that page is currently unpublished, so this link 404s until the box
  arrives and the page is published. That is expected and is why this theme must
  not be published yet (§8.1).

  Price card carries NO struck-through price, NO percentage, NO "save" language —
  removed deliberately for conflicting with §8.7. Do not reinstate.

  2026-09-05 — §8.7 OVERRIDE, deliberate, merchant-authorised. The line above is
  reversed for the price card ONLY: it now shows the Discovery Box's compare-at
  price struck through beside the live price. This is a decision, not a
  violation — do not silently revert it, and do not extend it to other sections.

  It is NOT hardcoded copy. The card reads price and compare_at_price straight
  off the RAQI Discovery Box variant, the same source the builder total on
  /pages/discovery-box reads, so the two can never disagree. Change the discount
  by editing compare-at on the product; clear compare-at and this card falls
  back to the offer_price setting and the single-price form, untouched.

  2026-09-14 — FRAME SIZING, deliberate, merchant-authorised. The paragraph
  below previously read that .rd-hero__frame and .rd-hero__panel had NOT been
  altered. That is no longer true and the record is corrected here rather than
  left to mislead a future cleanup pass.

  The 2026-09-05 re-crop remains the right call and was not undone: the image
  is still raqi_discovery_box_square_edge.jpg, 1200x1200, untouched. What was
  wrong was the container. The frame was capped at max-inline-size 340px inside
  a panel column measuring 634x848 at a 1280px viewport, so the photograph
  covered only 21.5% of its panel and read as a small picture adrift in a large
  beige field. object-fit: cover meant the image always filled its own frame
  exactly — the empty space was entirely panel padding plus that 340px cap,
  never a gap between image and frame.

  Changed in assets/raqi-redesign.css, not here: on <=900px the panel's fixed
  block-size: 340px -> auto with padding 32px -> 24px and the frame cap
  240px -> 560px, so the square drives the panel height instead of being
  letterboxed inside it; on desktop the panel padding went 64px -> 0 and the
  frame cap was removed entirely (max-inline-size: none), so the photograph
  spans the full width of its grid column. max-block-size: 100% is kept as an
  overflow guard for the case where short copy lets the panel fall back to
  .rd-hero's min-block-size. Frame coverage is now 74.7% on desktop, 67.2% at
  768px and 76-78% on phones, up from 21.5% / 22.1% / 41-45%.

  The frame stays 1:1, matching the 1200x1200 source exactly, so nothing is
  cropped and nothing is letterboxed. The residual panel colour above and below
  the image on desktop is inherent to fitting a square into a taller column, not
  slack in the frame.

  The srcset/sizes below were widened in the same change because the frame now
  renders up to 634 CSS px; the old 800w ceiling would have gone soft on retina.
  1200w is the ceiling because that is the source's native width -- asking for
  more would claim a width Shopify cannot actually serve.

  The rest of the section remains LOCKED.

  Everything is an editable setting so copy, price and image can be changed from
  the theme customizer without a developer.
{% endcomment %}
{% render 'rd-fonts' %}
<div class="rd-scope">
  <a class="rd-hero" href="{{ section.settings.link | default: '/pages/discovery-box' }}">
    <div class="rd-hero__copy">
      {%- liquid
        # 2026-09-14 -- locale keys for the hero copy, merchant-authorised. The
        # setting still wins when it carries a value, exactly as
        # sections/raqi-product.liquid does it, so the customizer keeps working
        # as an override. When the setting is blank the raqi.rd.hero.* key is
        # used, and THAT is what makes the copy translatable: these three
        # strings are section settings, and section settings are not
        # locale-aware -- writing Arabic into locales/ar.json does nothing for
        # them unless they are routed through `| t` like this.
        #
        # templates/index.json ships these three settings blank on purpose. Type
        # anything into the customizer fields and you pin that text for EVERY
        # language, English and Arabic alike. To change hero copy, edit
        # locales/en.default.json and locales/ar.json instead.
        assign hero_eyebrow = section.settings.eyebrow
        if hero_eyebrow == blank
          assign hero_eyebrow = 'raqi.rd.hero.eyebrow' | t
        endif
        assign hero_heading = section.settings.heading
        if hero_heading == blank
          assign hero_heading = 'raqi.rd.hero.heading' | t
        endif
        assign hero_body = section.settings.body
        if hero_body == blank
          assign hero_body = 'raqi.rd.hero.body' | t
        endif
      -%}
      <p class="rd-hero__eyebrow">{{ hero_eyebrow }}</p>
      <h1 class="rd-hero__h1">{{ hero_heading }}</h1>
      <p class="rd-hero__body">{{ hero_body }}</p>

      {%- if section.settings.show_offer -%}
        {%- liquid
          # One handle lookup, no catalogue loop, so no 50-item cap exposure --
          # the same pattern sections/raqi-discovery-box.liquid uses. If the
          # product is missing or carries no compare-at, every branch below
          # falls back to the offer_price setting and the card looks exactly as
          # it did before this change.
          assign hero_box = all_products['raqi-discovery-box']
          assign hero_v = hero_box.variants.first
          assign hero_was = false
          if hero_v and hero_v.compare_at_price > hero_v.price
            assign hero_was = true
          endif
        -%}
        <div class="rd-hero__offer">
          {%- if hero_was -%}
            <s class="rd-hero__offer-was">{{ hero_v.compare_at_price | money_without_trailing_zeros }}</s>
            <span class="rd-hero__offer-price">{{ hero_v.price | money_without_trailing_zeros }}</span>
          {%- else -%}
            <span class="rd-hero__offer-price">{{ section.settings.offer_price }}</span>
          {%- endif -%}
          {%- if section.settings.offer_breakdown != blank -%}
            <p class="rd-hero__offer-break">{{ section.settings.offer_breakdown }}</p>
          {%- endif -%}
        </div>
      {%- endif -%}

      <div class="rd-hero__cta">
        {%- for block in section.blocks -%}
          {%- if block.type == 'cta' -%}
            {%- liquid
              assign klass = 'rd-btn rd-btn--ghost'
              assign cta_key = 'raqi.rd.hero.cta_secondary'
              if block.settings.style == 'primary'
                assign klass = 'rd-btn rd-btn--primary'
                assign cta_key = 'raqi.rd.hero.cta_primary'
              endif
              # Same override-then-key pattern as the copy above. The key is
              # chosen by button style, not by block order, so reordering the
              # blocks in the customizer cannot swap the two labels.
              assign cta_label = block.settings.label
              if cta_label == blank
                assign cta_label = cta_key | t
              endif
            -%}
            <span class="{{ klass }}" {{ block.shopify_attributes }}>{{ cta_label }}</span>
          {%- endif -%}
        {%- endfor -%}
      </div>

      {%- if section.settings.step_line != blank -%}
        <p class="rd-hero__steps">{{ 'raqi.rd.hero.try_it' | t }} <span>&rarr;</span> {{ 'raqi.rd.hero.live_with_it' | t }} <span>&rarr;</span> {{ 'raqi.rd.hero.decide' | t }}</p>
      {%- endif -%}
    </div>

    <div class="rd-hero__panel">
      <div class="rd-hero__frame">
        {%- if section.settings.image != blank -%}
          <img src="{{ section.settings.image | image_url: width: 1200 }}"
               srcset="{{ section.settings.image | image_url: width: 400 }} 400w, {{ section.settings.image | image_url: width: 640 }} 640w, {{ section.settings.image | image_url: width: 900 }} 900w, {{ section.settings.image | image_url: width: 1200 }} 1200w"
               sizes="(max-width: 900px) min(100vw - 48px, 560px), min(50vw, 634px)"
               alt="{{ section.settings.image_alt | escape }}"
               width="{{ section.settings.image.width }}" height="{{ section.settings.image.height }}"
               loading="eager" fetchpriority="high">
        {%- else -%}
          <span class="rd-hero__oval" aria-hidden="true">
            <span class="rd-hero__oval-en">RAQI</span>
            <span class="rd-hero__oval-ar" lang="ar">راقي</span>
          </span>
          <span class="rd-hero__bottles" aria-hidden="true">
            <span class="rd-hero__bottle"></span><span class="rd-hero__bottle"></span><span class="rd-hero__bottle"></span>
          </span>
          <span class="rd-visually-hidden">{{ section.settings.image_alt }}</span>
        {%- endif -%}
      </div>
    </div>
  </a>
</div>

{% style %}
  /* 2026-09-05 — §8.7 override, see the header. The ONLY style added to this
     locked section, and it introduces no new component: it styles the struck
     figure alone. --rd-ink (#22261F) on the card's --rd-panel ground (#E8EBE2)
     is about 12:1, so the old price reads as a real number being crossed out
     rather than the faint grey-on-grey these cards usually get. */
  .rd-hero__offer-was {
    display: block;
    font-family: var(--rd-body);
    font-size: 15px;
    letter-spacing: .04em;
    color: var(--rd-ink);
    text-decoration: line-through;
    text-decoration-thickness: 1px;
    margin-block-end: 6px;
  }
  @media (max-width: 900px) {
    .rd-hero__offer-was { font-size: 13px; }
  }
{% endstyle %}

{% schema %}
{
  "name": "RD Hero",
  "tag": "section",
  "max_blocks": 3,
  "settings": [
    { "type": "url", "id": "link", "label": "Hero link", "info": "The whole hero is one click target. Defaults to the Discovery Set builder." },
    { "type": "text", "id": "eyebrow", "label": "Eyebrow", "default": "RAQI Discovery Set" },
    { "type": "text", "id": "heading", "label": "Headline", "default": "No one should buy a signature in two minutes." },
    { "type": "textarea", "id": "body", "label": "Body", "default": "Choose 1 Signature + 2 Discovery fragrances — 15ml each, 45ml total. Experience three original fragrances before committing to a full bottle." },
    { "type": "text", "id": "step_line", "label": "Show step line", "default": "yes", "info": "Clear this field to hide the Try it → Live with it → Decide line." },
    { "type": "header", "content": "Price card" },
    { "type": "checkbox", "id": "show_offer", "label": "Show price card", "default": true },
    { "type": "text", "id": "offer_price", "label": "Price (fallback only)", "default": "Dhs. 599", "info": "Shown only if the RAQI Discovery Box product is missing. Normally the card reads the live price and compare-at price from that product's variant." },
    { "type": "text", "id": "offer_breakdown", "label": "Detail line", "default": "Three fragrances · 45ml · Individually Dhs. 850" },
    { "type": "header", "content": "Image" },
    { "type": "image_picker", "id": "image", "label": "Discovery Set box photograph", "info": "Pending from the manufacturer. Until set, the placeholder frame renders — never stock photography." },
    { "type": "text", "id": "image_alt", "label": "Alt text", "default": "The RAQI Discovery Set box" }
  ],
  "blocks": [
    { "type": "cta", "name": "Button", "settings": [
      { "type": "text", "id": "label", "label": "Label", "default": "Build Your Set" },
      { "type": "select", "id": "style", "label": "Style", "default": "primary",
        "options": [ { "value": "primary", "label": "Filled (wine)" }, { "value": "secondary", "label": "Outlined" } ] }
    ] }
  ],
  "presets": [{ "name": "RD Hero" }]
}
{% endschema %}
